<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pha Mueang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Pho Khun Pha Mueang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pha Mueang, or Pho Khun Pha Mueang, was a Tai chief of Mueang Rat in north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> in the thirteenth century. According to a Sukhothai inscription, he joined forces with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/si-inthrathit">Bang Klang Hao</a> to expel the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> governor of Sukhothai, around the conventional date of 1238, after which Bang Klang Hao became the first king of Sukhothai as Si Inthrathit.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pha-mueang.jpg" alt="Pha Mueang" width="250" height="351" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tongsuk2536 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%9B%E0%B8%9E%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9C%E0%B8%B2%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B7%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%87_%E0%B8%84%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%9E%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9C%E0%B8%B2%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B7%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%87_%E0%B8%88%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%8A%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
